/-!
# Finitely presented invariant rank filtration of a finite groupoid

Source: Stacks Project, More on Groupoids, Tags 0AB9 and 0ABB, first proof paragraph
(blueprint: lem-sfb-finite-presented-groupoid-rank-filtration).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A finite groupoid of finite presentation has an invariant closed rank filtration whose
closed immersions are finitely presented. Closed subschemes are represented by their ideal
sheaves; increasing ideals give decreasing closed subschemes. The stratum of degree `n + 1`
is the open complement of `Z (n + 1)` inside `Z n`.
Source: Stacks Project, More on Groupoids, Tags 0AB9 and 0ABB, first proof paragraph
(blueprint: lem-sfb-finite-presented-groupoid-rank-filtration).

Proof plan, in the order of the node's eight steps:
1. Set `E = s_* O_R` and `J n = Fit_n(E)`, using
   `lem-trf-fitting-ideal-sheaf-pullback`. Laplace expansion gives `J n ≤ J (n + 1)`.
   Finite generation on affine opens (`lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-finite-type-affine`)
   makes some `J n` the unit ideal locally, giving empty intersection of supports.
2. The identity section splits the affine structure map `A → B`. For any square matrix
   of kernel rows of a generating presentation of `B`, its adjugate shows that its
   determinant kills every generator, hence `1`. Injectivity of `A → B` makes this
   determinant zero. Thus `Fit_0(E) = 0`, including on the empty affine open.
3. The source-pullback translation of `lem-a1-groupoid-source-pullback-translation`
   identifies `R ×[s,U,t] R` with `R ×[s,U,s] R` over their second factors.
   The algebra clause of `lem-weil-pbc-affine-pushforward-base-change` identifies
   `t^*E` and `s^*E`.
4. Fitting pullback and invariance under module isomorphism make `J n.comap s` and
   `J n.comap t` equal, giving equality of closed subschemes, including nilpotents.
5. On the complement of `Z r`, `lem-trf-fitting-ideal-generate-locally` bounds the
   number of generators by `r`. On `Z (r - 1)` its preceding Fitting ideal vanishes.
   Apply `lem-sfb-bounded-generators-fitting-pullback-criterion` to get rank `r`.
6. Affine permanence and affine pushforward base change identify the restricted source
   algebra with this rank-`r` module. On trivializing affine opens use
   `lem-weil-pbc-finite-free-algebra-spectrum` and `lem-pc-finite-affine-fibre-sections`.
   Open immersions are etale, so `lem-weil-pbc-finite-locally-free-degree-etale-descent`
   gives degree `r` on the whole stratum, including the empty stratum.
7. On each affine open, finite presentation of `s` gives a finitely presented algebra.
   `lem-weil-pbc-finite-algebra-presentation-module-presentation` gives a finite module
   presentation with a finite matrix of relations; no global bound is needed.
8. Expand minors of arbitrary relation rows multilinearly in the finite generating
   rows. Repeated row indices vanish; the remaining determinants are, up to sign,
   minors of that finite matrix. Thus every Fitting ideal is finitely generated locally
   (and is generated by `1` above the generator bound). Apply
   `lem-trf-closed-immersion-finite-presentation-ideal` to obtain finite presentation.
-/
theorem groupoid_exists_finitePresentation_rank_filtration
    {U R : Scheme.{u}} (s t : R ⟶ U) (e : U ⟶ R) (i : R ⟶ R)
    (c : pullback s t ⟶ R) (hG : IsGroupoidScheme s t e i c)
    [IsFinite s] [IsFinite t]
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation s] [LocallyOfFinitePresentation t] :
    ∃ J : ℕ → U.IdealSheafData,
      J 0 = ⊥ ∧ Monotone J ∧
      (⋂ n : ℕ, ((J n).support : Set U)) = ∅ ∧
      (∀ n : ℕ, LocallyOfFinitePresentation (J n).subschemeι ∧
        QuasiCompact (J n).subschemeι ∧ QuasiSeparated (J n).subschemeι) ∧
      (∀ n : ℕ, (J n).comap s = (J n).comap t) ∧
      ∀ n : ℕ,
        (pullback.snd s
          ((Scheme.Opens.ι ((J n).subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ (J (n + 1)).support.compl)) ≫
            (J n).subschemeι)).IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfDegree (n + 1) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
